# Knowing where other aircraft are (domains/communication). The station only has the TX15's
# telemetry. Other aircraft reach it in two ways: a Remote ID receiver on the pilot's plane
# hears their broadcasts, and a MAVLink network carries their positions. Both go down the
# radio link with the pilot's own plane. The tests run on the communication domain with no
# window: a simulated radio medium, the TX15's downlink and the station's tracker. See
# domains/communication/radio/tests/acceptance.rs.

Section: Other aircraft
  The station shows the other aircraft near your plane on the [[tactical map]]. It does not
  see them itself. The station only gets the telemetry that the TX15 radio passes on. Your
  plane tells the station about the other aircraft that it can hear.

  There are two sources. Your plane has a [[Remote ID]] receiver. It hears the aircraft that
  broadcast Remote ID, and only the aircraft that are near. Your plane is also on a
  [[MAVLink]] network with other pilots. Each plane on the network shares its position, and
  the network has a longer range. The station joins what it hears into one marker for each
  aircraft.

Vocabulary:
  State: the other plane is silent | sending Remote ID | sending MAVLink | sending both
    Set: ask the other pilot to be {value}
    Shows: silent: the other plane has no marker after a while
    Shows: sending Remote ID: the other plane broadcasts its position and its ID
    Shows: sending MAVLink: the other plane shares its position on the MAVLink network
    Shows: sending both: the other plane broadcasts Remote ID and shares its position on the MAVLink network
  State: the distance to the other plane is 0..8000 m
    Set: ask the other pilot to fly {value} from your plane
    Shows: the marker of the other plane is {value} from the marker of your plane
  State: the map has 0..40 other planes
    Shows: the number of markers of other planes on the tactical map is {value}
  State: the marker of the other plane is missing | live | stale
    Shows: missing: the map has no marker for the other plane
    Shows: live: the marker is bright, and it moves with the other plane
    Shows: stale: the marker is dim, and it stays where the other plane was last heard
  State: the source of the marker is none | Remote ID | MAVLink | Remote ID and MAVLink
    Shows: Remote ID: the label of the marker says RID
    Shows: MAVLink: the label of the marker says MAV
    Shows: Remote ID and MAVLink: the label of the marker says MAV RID
  State: the TX15 link is up | lost
    Shows: lost: the LINK annunciator flashes
  State: your Remote ID is on | off
    Shows: on: the transmitter on your plane broadcasts the ID and the position of your plane
  State: the crowd has 0..40 planes
    Set: ask {value} more pilots to share their positions on the MAVLink network
    Shows: the map gets {value} more markers
  State: the telemetry of your plane has 0..20 position updates per second
    Shows: at least 4: the marker of your plane moves smoothly, and the flight display does not freeze

  Event: 5 seconds pass
    Say: wait 5 seconds
  Event: 10 seconds pass
    Say: wait 10 seconds
  Event: 70 seconds pass
    Say: wait one minute and 10 seconds

  Phrase: the station is connected to the TX15
    Say: switch on the TX15 and the plane. Start the station. The map shows your plane, and no other planes
    Given the TX15 link is up
    And your Remote ID is on
    And the other plane is silent
    And the distance to the other plane is 200 m
    And the crowd has 0 planes
    And the map has 0 other planes

Background:
  Given the station is connected to the TX15
